  "notes": [
    "Time: every instant is its calendar value read as UT1 (DUT1 = 0, the same assumption as LodestarKit's JulianDate(date:)); TT = UT1 + DeltaT with DeltaT from Skyfield's builtin tables (IERS daily values 1973-01-02..2027-01-23, Stephenson/Morrison/Hohenkerk splines and parabola elsewhere). No IERS download, no polar motion.",
    "phases: every new moon, first quarter, full moon and last quarter with 2024-01-01 <= instant < 2029-01-01, from skyfield.almanac.moon_phases: the instants where the geocentric apparent ecliptic longitude of the Moon minus that of the Sun (true ecliptic of date) is 0, 90, 180, 270 degrees, resolved to 1 ms. 'utc' is the instant read as UT1; 'unix' is POSIX seconds of that same calendar value.",
    "samples.illuminated_fraction, samples.phase_angle_deg: geocentric; phase_angle_deg is the Sun-Moon-Earth angle at the Moon (0 = full, 180 = new) and illuminated_fraction = (1 + cos(phase_angle_deg)) / 2.",
    "samples.ecliptic_elongation_deg: Skyfield almanac.moon_phase, the apparent ecliptic longitude of the Moon minus that of the Sun in [0, 360): 0 new, 90 first quarter, 180 full, 270 last quarter; the Moon is waxing while it is below 180.",
    "samples.age_days: days since the preceding new moon of the 'phases' list (the file also searches one lunation before the first listed phase)."
  ],
